# Proposed by the swarm's review (2026-10-14), from the product owner's replay; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: five windows arranged, so the Desktop is a tile. A new window opens over them and is being typed in. Somebody
# minimizes another window and brings it back. The Desktop is wide enough to use for that moment. The window being typed
# in must neither be squeezed onto it nor go out of view when it is a tile again.
# Reference: T03 T07 T52.
open A
open B
open C
open D
open E
arrange
open F 500x400
expect visible 106
minimize 105
expect visible 106
restore 105
expect visible 106
expect floating 106
